(:taskCollection
  :id "Phase471ClosingTheUnplanned"
  :createdAt 1789320000000
  :status "done"
  :priorityOrder 2
  :summary "Closing the Unplanned: the three findings and requests from this programme that no task covers, being the declared python3 dependency, the agent authoring and scaffolding path, and the plan verification that exists only in a session scratchpad."
  :phase "Phase471ClosingTheUnplanned"
  :baseline "Gap analysed 2026-09-12 by matching every finding and request of this programme against the text of Phase436 through Phase470. Thirty three of thirty six are covered. Three are not. python3 remains declared at .asl/mem/dependencies.asn:29 and no task in the programme owns that file, although its removal was one of the six actions of a remediation phase already marked complete. Agent authoring and scaffolding was requested explicitly and appears in the current programme nowhere; the only occurrence in the whole task ledger is Phase414. Plan verification, being the DAG acyclicity check, the D52 field completeness check and the unordered writer pair computation that produced the 529 and 1309 figures quoted throughout this programme, exists only as scripts in a session scratchpad and will not survive the session; nothing under tests or scripts verifies the plan."
  :tasks [
    (:task
      :id "Task47101" :parentId "" :phase "phase-471"
      :title "The plan is verified by the repository, not by a scratchpad"
      :kind :tooling :state :done :lane "closure" :priority :critical :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789320000000 :updatedAt 1789320000000
      :motivation "Every structural claim this programme has made about its own plan came from scripts in a session scratchpad: that the DAG is acyclic, that no task is missing a D52 field, that every task is registered in the ADR and the intent and the decision ledgers, and that 529 pairs of tasks write a common path without an ordering. None of those checks is in the repository, so the next session inherits the numbers and not the ability to reproduce them. This is the same defect as the sweep scripts, arriving for the plan instead of the code."
      :purpose "Plan verification is a command in the repository: it reads the phase files, reports cycles, missing fields, unregistered tasks, dangling dependencies and unordered writer pairs, and fails on any. It runs when a phase is registered, so a plan defect is caught where it is introduced rather than in a later audit."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Plan verification as a repository command" "Cycles, missing fields, unregistered tasks and writer pairs reported" "Runs at registration" "The quoted figures reproducible without the session"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c" "tests/acceptance/d81"]
      :targetSymbols ["run_audit_consistency"] :relatedSymbols ["parallel" "anchor" "gates"]
      :invariants ["D52" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task45803"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47101"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47101.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A task introducing a dependency cycle fails the check, naming the cycle." "A task missing a mandatory field fails, naming the field." "A task depending on an identifier that exists nowhere fails." "The unordered writer pair count it reports matches an independent computation on the same tree."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47101" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Port the checks into the binary." "Run at registration." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 3 :receipts ["rc-task47101-verified-20260912"])
    (:task
      :id "Task47102" :parentId "" :phase "phase-471"
      :title "Authoring and scaffolding as a first class agent path"
      :kind :tooling :state :done :lane "closure" :priority :high :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789320000000 :updatedAt 1789320000000
      :motivation "An agent that can read, plan and remember but must author code by writing whole files is doing the most error prone part of its work with the least support. Scaffolding was asked for explicitly and appears in the current programme nowhere. The material for it exists: structural_editor, ast_merge, ast_filter and the five editing modalities the implementer mandate already names, of which the staged ones do not yet stage."
      :purpose "An agent creates a module, a function or a test from the shapes the language already defines, so a new artefact starts valid rather than being made valid. Edits are staged and reviewable before they reach disk, since the mandate already promises staging that the engine does not provide. A scaffold produces something that parses, binds and carries its own negative case, because a scaffold that produces a stub is how the constant returning bodies already in the corpus got there."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Scaffolds for module, function and test" "Staged edits that can be reviewed before landing" "A scaffold never emits a constant returning body" "The promised editing modalities made real"]
      :owns ["mem/src/structural_editor.asl" "asl/tools/asl.c" "asl/grammar/rpc.asn"]
      :targetSymbols ["structural_editor" "ast_merge"] :relatedSymbols ["tools" "oneStep" "gates"]
      :invariants ["C1" "C3" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task46501" "Task46102"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47102"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47102.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A scaffolded module parses, binds and executes at least one assertion without hand repair." "A staged edit is visible before it lands and can be discarded without touching disk." "A scaffold emitting a constant returning body fails its own check."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47102" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Define the scaffolds." "Make staging real." "Refuse stub output." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 4 :receipts ["rc-task47102-verified-20260912"])
    (:task
      :id "Task47103" :parentId "" :phase "phase-471"
      :title "The dependency ledger says what is actually required"
      :kind :remediation :state :done :lane "closure" :priority :moderate :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789320000000 :updatedAt 1789320000000
      :motivation "python3 is declared at .asl/mem/dependencies.asn:29 and its removal was one of six actions in a remediation phase already marked complete. The generator it was removed from no longer uses it, so the declaration outlived the dependency, and no task in this programme owns that file. A dependency ledger that lists what used to be needed is worse than none, because it is the document a portability decision would be made from."
      :purpose "Every entry in the dependency ledger is verified to be actually required by something the build or the deployed runtime uses, and an entry that nothing requires is removed. Declared boundaries such as a seed compiler or an independent test host are distinguished from runtime requirements, since the foreign rule treats them differently."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Every declared dependency verified as required" "Unused entries removed" "Build boundaries distinguished from runtime requirements" "The ledger usable for a portability decision"]
      :owns [".asl/mem/dependencies.asn" "asl/grammar/dependency-boundaries.asn"]
      :targetSymbols [] :relatedSymbols ["foreign" "concepts"]
      :invariants ["D34" "D81"] :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes) :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081" :decision "d81" :dependsOn ["Task46404"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47103"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier" :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task47103.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A declared dependency that nothing invokes is reported." "Removing a real dependency breaks a build step and is caught." "A build boundary is not counted as a runtime requirement."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task47103" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts [] :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Verify each entry against use." "Remove the unused." "Separate boundaries from requirements." "Independent acceptance."] :stepIndex 4 :receipts ["rc-task47103-verified-20260912"])]
  :notes "Found by matching every finding and request of this programme against the text of Phase436 through Phase470: thirty three of thirty six covered, these three not. Task47101 matters most, because without it the next session inherits this programme's numbers and not the means to check them.")
